\f0\fs32 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 Yes \'97 this helps a lot, and it\'92s exactly the right \'93instrument-first\'94 correction.\cb1 \
\
\cb3 What\'92s good (and aligned with our current work)\cb1 \
\cb3 You correctly reject running \uc0\u964  on the z-axis. \u964  is a time constant; the kernel must live in time.\cb1 \
\cb3 You correctly insist on a standard H(z)H(z)\cb1 \
\cb3 H(z) mapping so nobody can accuse you of \'93cooking the transform.\'94\cb1 \
\cb3 You correctly pause for the Vault before pointing at sky data (now we can publish immutable receipts).\cb1 \
\cb3 So: 
\f12 \AppleTypeServices \uc0\u9989 
\f0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539  we should implement the z
\f11 \AppleTypeServices \uc0\u8594 
\f0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 t adapter next, then wire it into an endpoint that feeds the existing, validated Anamnesis search_tau.\cb1 \
\cb3 Two key implementation choices (to keep it sovereign + lightweight)\cb1 \
\cb3 Use the standard lookback-time integrand\cb1 \
\
\cb3 If we\'92re mapping redshift to time, use:\cb1 \
\cb3 tL(z)=\uc0\u8747 0zdz\u8242 (1+z\u8242 )\u8201 H(z\u8242 )t_L(z) = \\int_0^z \\frac\{dz'\}\{(1+z')\\,H(z')\}\cb1 \
\cb3 tL\cb1 \
\cb3 (z)=\uc0\u8747 0\cb1 \
\cb3 z\cb1 \
\cb3 (1+z\uc0\u8242 \cb1 \
\cb3 )H(z\uc0\u8242 \cb1 \
\cb3 )\cb1 \
\cb3 dz\uc0\u8242 \cb1 \
\
\cb3 This is the clean cosmology mapping (more correct than integrating only 1/E(z)1/E(z)\cb1 \
\cb3 1/E(z) without the (1+z)(1+z)\cb1 \
\cb3 (1+z) factor).\cb1 \
\
\cb3 Avoid SciPy in runtime if possible\cb1 \
\
\cb3 SciPy is fine, but it\'92s heavy. You can do this with pure NumPy:\cb1 \
\cb3 compute cumulative integral with trapezoid rule over z grid\cb1 \
\cb3 resample with np.interp (linear) to a uniform dt grid\cb1 \
\
\cb3 Later, spline interpolation can be an optional \'93dev\'94 upgrade.\cb1 \
\cb3 This preserves your \'93cold instrument\'94 posture.\cb1 \
\cb3 Paste this to VS AI: Real Data Adapter + fsigma8 \uc0\u964 -search endpoint (instrument-only)\cb1 \
\cb3 Implement data_adapter.py (z
\f11 \AppleTypeServices \uc0\u8594 
\f0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 t) and /anamnesis/search_tau_fsigma8 using existing Anamnesis search_tau. No ontology logic.\cb1 \
\
\cb3 1) Add core/data_adapter.py\cb1 \
\cb3 Use LCDM mapping with parameters (\uc0\u937 m, \u937 \u923 , H0)\cb1 \
\cb3 Provide:\cb1 \
\cb3 hz_lcdm(z, H0, Om, Ol)\cb1 \
\cb3 lookback_time_gyr(z_array, H0, Om, Ol) using cumulative trapezoid of 1/((1+z)E(z))\cb1 \
\cb3 resample_uniform(t_gyr, y, dt_gyr) using np.interp\cb1 \
\cb3 conversions: Gyr 
\f13 \AppleTypeServices \uc0\u8596 
\f0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539  seconds (for kernel dt_s, tau_s)\cb1 \
\cb3 Important: sort z, map to time, ensure monotonicity.\cb1 \
\
\cb3 2) Add schemas in core/schemas.py\cb1 \
\cb3 Create:\cb1 \
\
\cb3 Fsigma8DatasetRequest:\cb1 \
\cb3 z: List[float]\cb1 \
\cb3 fsigma8: List[float]\cb1 \
\cb3 sigma: Optional[List[float]] (errors)\cb1 \
\cb3 dataset_label: Optional[str]\cb1 \
\cb3 cosmo: \{H0_km_s_Mpc, Omega_m\} (defaults Planck-like; Omega_L = 1-Om)\cb1 \
\cb3 Fsigma8TauSearchRequest:\cb1 \
\cb3 data: Fsigma8DatasetRequest\cb1 \
\cb3 dt_myr: float = 5.0 (default resample step in Myr; adjustable)\cb1 \
